  Unfortunately for the DevTeam, people are enjoying Nethack the 
way they want.  People already enjoy Nethack multiplayer.  
(Saying Nethack is just for nerds with no social skills would be 
a sad commentary on Nethack.)

  Playing Nethack multiplayer (as some folks already do) has no
different requirements from AD&D, Monopoly(TM), Sorry!, checkers,
chess, etc.  Nethack players are at least as clever as two
children playing checkers, IMHO.

  What was the round-robin if not multi-player nethack?  Or 
playing on nao chatting on irc with people watching your game?
(That last is going on constantly.)

  So people play Nethack multiplayer regardless of the DevTeam's 
wishes.  Just as players re-roll, ignore ascending, savescum, 
hack the source, and even invent their own conducts (zen) without
consulting the DevTeam.

  Multi-character Nethack might enhance Nethack's multi-player
affinity.  It might not.  Adding the ability to control a single
pet, with balancing weaknesses, would be an exciting direction
for Nethack.  It might fail miserably.  It might kill Nethack 
dead, leaving us to play v3.4.3 for years. (Just like we're doing
now.)  I don't see how it could kill Nethack.  Slash'EM didn't.
